      <title>
        <![CDATA[ Energy drinks are for the girls ]]>
      </title>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[ <p>Energy drinks are for the girls: a deep dive into the drink that's all of a sudden everywhere!</p><p>In this episode of 'The Curious Consumer,' hosts Nate and Jenna explore the evolving energy drink market, discussing everything from nostalgic brands like Red Bull and Monster to newcomers like Celsius and Bloom. They delve into historical origins, from Japan's early energy tonics to Red Bull's global dominance, and highlight current trends such as lower caffeine options, natural ingredients, and gendered marketing. Listeners will also learn about recent industry acquisitions, emerging ingredients, and predictions for the future of energy drinks. The episode ends with a teaser for the next discussion on the commodification of sleep.</p><p>00:00 Introduction</p><p>02:24 Seasonal Products and Pumpkin Spice</p><p>06:13 Current News: Starbucks Protein Cold Foam Launch</p><p>08:45 Current News: Erewhon Coming to New York</p><p>16:53 History of Energy Drinks</p><p>22:42 The Rise of Celsius</p><p>25:52 Marketing Energy Drinks to Women</p><p>35:19 New Trends in Energy Drinks</p><p>45:12 The Future of Energy Drinks</p><p>49:04 Closing Thoughts</p> <br/><br/>Get full access to Express Checkout at <a href="https://expresscheckout.co/subscribe?utm_medium=podcast&#38;utm_campaign=CTA_4">expresscheckout.co/subscribe</a> ]]>
